<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi Rajhi Banking 1996 net income rises.</title>
<headline>Saudi Rajhi Banking 1996 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			 (million Saudi riyals)</p>
<p> Net income		1,208.2    vs    1,117.4</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	  1,240.1    vs    1,148.1</p>
<p> Provision		   275.4    vs	227.0</p>
<p> Dividend		    900.0    vs	750.0</p>
<p> Operating cost	  1,048.1    vs	938.5</p>
<p> Operating income	2,288.3    vs    2,086.6</p>
<p> Shareholders' equity  4,759.8    vs    4,451.6</p>
<p> Assets		   32,281.6    vs   30,662.6</p>
<p>Full Name: Al-Rajhi Banking and Investment Corporation.</p>
<p>Note - The Riyadh-based bank enjoys a good reputation among ordinary Saudis due to its stated commitment to Islamic law, which bans payment and receipt of interest. -- Manama newsroom +973 536187</p>
</text>
